cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or its result files, please cite the report below.
  The report is an extended research report and has not been peer reviewed.
title: "MTPI-Bench and CASA: code for a conversation-level defence against multi-turn prompt injection"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mukherjee
    given-names: Ritesh
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - prompt injection
  - multi-turn attacks
  - large language models
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - adversarial training
  - LoRA
  - direct preference optimisation
abstract: >-
  Research code for an extended research report on defending locally deployed
  language models against prompt injection that is spread over several
  conversational turns or delivered inside retrieved content. It contains the
  build script for the MTPI-Bench benchmark, a turn-level detector grid, the
  conversation-level detector CASA, an adaptive attacker with symmetric
  adversarial training, a LoRA-DPO alignment study, a live
  retrieval-augmented-generation evaluation, and the result files behind the
  tables of the report.
preferred-citation:
  type: report
  title: >-
    Conversation-Level Defence Against Multi-Turn Prompt Injection in Locally
    Deployed Large Language Models: Sequential Evidence Accumulation,
    Provenance Separation and Detector-Supervised Preference Alignment
  authors:
    - family-names: Mukherjee
      given-names: Ritesh
  year: 2026
  month: 10
  notes: >-
    Extended research report. An extension of the author's MSc dissertation;
    not the dissertation submitted for the degree. Not peer reviewed.
